{"id": "2026-11-20-news-russian-missiles-cut-kyiv-s-dnipro-bridges", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russian missiles cut Kyiv's Dnipro bridges", "summary": "Russian missile and drone strikes overnight into 20 November hit three Kyiv bridges and killed eight people in Ukraine, six in the capital.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/20/russia-unleashes-retaliatory-barrage-on-kyiv-bridges", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Russia struck Kyiv's bridges over the Dnipro with ballistic missiles and drones overnight into Friday 20 November, killing eight people across Ukraine, six of them in the capital, and wounding 28, Prime Minister Sergii Koretskyi said. Kyiv mayor Vitali Klitschko said the Podilskyi, Darnytskyi and Southern bridges were hit; RFI's correspondent reports that two of the city's five main bridges are now closed and a third cannot carry heavy lorries, and Klitschko told residents to stay home. Power was cut across the city, and nuclear plants elsewhere had to reduce output, causing outages in Kyiv and ten regions, according to Ukraine's energy ministry. Russia's defence ministry said the bridges were used to move weapons to the front. The strikes came hours after Vladimir Putin, speaking in China on Thursday, promised a \"painful\" response to Ukraine's attacks this week on the Crimean Bridge, which cut its road link.", "why": "the Dnipro splits Kyiv in two, with about half its people on each bank, so hitting the bridges is meant to cut the city apart going into what Volodymyr Zelensky calls the hardest winter of the war. It also came the morning after the Xi–Trump–Putin summit in Shenzhen, which produced no ceasefire.", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-russian-missiles-cut-kyiv-s-dnipro-bridges", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Kyiv", "Vladimir Putin", "Crimean Bridge"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-uk-and-eu-conclude-post-brexit-reset-deal", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "UK and EU conclude post-Brexit reset deal", "summary": "Downing Street said the UK and EU concluded a reset deal on food trade, emissions trading and youth mobility at their 20 November Brussels summit.", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/20/uk-eu-european-union-brexit-deal-andy-burnham-latest-news-updates", "source_domain": "theguardian.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The United Kingdom and the European Union concluded a deal to \"reset\" their relations at a summit in Brussels on Friday 20 November, Downing Street said, covering food and plant trade, emissions trading and a youth mobility scheme. \"The deal is done – negotiations have concluded,\" a spokesperson for Prime Minister Andy Burnham said, adding that talks \"will continue on some areas\" and that start dates will be in a joint statement not yet published. The EU side has said the deal will not take effect without a later agreement on the tuition fees EU students pay at British universities. Ahead of the summit, reporting put the youth scheme at 100,000 places each way, for stays of up to three years, and Britain valued ending food and plant border checks at about £5.1 billion a year. Reform UK leader Nigel Farage called it a Brexit \"betrayal\".", "why": "this is the first broad rebuild of UK–EU ties since Brexit, and it is made of sector deals, like those Switzerland already has with the EU, at the moment Bern is debating the Bilaterals III package. How Brussels handles the UK's terms will be watched in the Swiss debate.", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-uk-and-eu-conclude-post-brexit-reset-deal", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United Kingdom", "European Union", "Andy Burnham", "Ursula von der Leyen"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-turkish-court-ends-i-mamo-lu-s-presidential-path", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "Turkish court ends İmamoğlu's presidential path", "summary": "Turkey's Council of State upheld the revocation of Ekrem İmamoğlu's university degree on 19 November, barring him from the 2028 presidential race.", "url": "https://www.tagesschau.de/ausland/europa/tuerkei-imamoglu-104.html", "source_domain": "tagesschau.de", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Turkey's Council of State, the highest administrative court, upheld the revocation of jailed Istanbul mayor Ekrem İmamoğlu's university degree on Thursday 19 November. Turkey's constitution requires presidential candidates to hold a degree, so the ruling bars İmamoğlu, the strongest rival of President Recep Tayyip Erdoğan, from the 2028 presidential election. Its 8th Chamber rejected his appeal after two lower courts had backed Istanbul University, which annulled the degree in March 2025, the day before his arrest and days before his party, the Republican People's Party (CHP), was to nominate him. He has been in jail for more than a year and a half and is on trial with 413 co-defendants on 142 charges, including corruption. İmamoğlu and his supporters say the government is behind the cases to keep him off the ballot.", "why": "it closes the administrative route to his candidacy, so Turkey's main opposition must now plan for 2028 without its most popular figure.", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-turkish-court-ends-i-mamo-lu-s-presidential-path", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-19", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Turkey", "Ekrem İmamoğlu", "Council of State", "Recep Tayyip Erdoğan", "CHP"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-cop31-draft-drops-fossil-fuel-phase-out", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "COP31 draft drops fossil-fuel phase-out", "summary": "COP31 reached its scheduled final day on 20 November without a deal after a draft removed explicit references to moving away from fossil fuels.", "url": "https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/11/1168839", "source_domain": "news.un.org", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The COP31 climate summit in Antalya, Turkey, reached its scheduled last day on Friday 20 November with no deal, after a new draft text dropped every explicit reference to moving away from coal, oil and gas. The draft, released on Thursday, does acknowledge that the world will overshoot the 1.5°C warming limit, UN News reports; talks on finance, adaptation and a \"just transition\" for workers remain unresolved. COP31 President Murat Kurum gathered ministers on Wednesday evening to try to break the deadlock, and ministers from vulnerable countries said little progress was made. As in past years, the talks are expected to run past the deadline.", "why": "the commitment to \"transition away from fossil fuels\" agreed at COP28 in Dubai was the main gain of recent summits. A final text without it would be a step back that campaigners already call a \"glaring regression\".", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-cop31-draft-drops-fossil-fuel-phase-out", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["COP31", "UNFCCC", "Turkey", "Murat Kurum"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-bukele-registers-for-a-third-term", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "Bukele registers for a third term", "summary": "Nayib Bukele registered on 19 November as a candidate for a third term in El Salvador's February 2027 election after term limits were removed.", "url": "https://www.rfi.fr/fr/am%C3%A9riques/20261120-salvador-le-pr%C3%A9sident-bukele-candidat-pour-un-troisi%C3%A8me-mandat-apr%C3%A8s-avoir-modifi%C3%A9-la-constitution", "source_domain": "rfi.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "El Salvador's President Nayib Bukele registered on Thursday 19 November as a candidate for a third term, in the February 2027 election, at the Supreme Electoral Tribunal. His party, Nuevas Ideas, used its supermajority in congress last year to change the constitution, removing presidential term limits and lengthening terms from five to six years. Bukele has about 80% approval, largely from his crackdown on gangs, which has sharply cut crime but which a UN expert group says has involved crimes against humanity. Critics, including the Bertelsmann Transformation Index, say he is building a de facto one-party state.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-bukele-registers-for-a-third-term", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-19", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["El Salvador", "Nayib Bukele", "Nuevas Ideas"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-pakistani-minister-visits-india-for-sco-forum", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "Pakistani minister visits India for SCO forum", "summary": "Pakistan's climate minister Musadik Malik arrived in New Delhi on 20 November for an SCO forum, the first ministerial visit since the May 2025 war.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news-analysis/2026/11/20/pakistan-minister-visits-india-for-first-time-since-2025-war", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Pakistan's climate minister, Musadik Malik, arrived in New Delhi on Friday 20 November, the first Pakistani federal minister to visit India since the two countries' four-day war in May 2025. He is attending a three-day Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO, a China- and Russia-led regional bloc) forum that Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi is due to open on Friday evening. No bilateral meeting has been announced, and both governments describe the visit as routine SCO business. Pakistan hosts the SCO leaders' summit next August.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-pakistani-minister-visits-india-for-sco-forum", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Pakistan", "India", "SCO", "Musadik Malik"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-vaud-committee-urges-rejecting-2027-budget", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "Vaud committee urges rejecting 2027 budget", "summary": "Vaud's Grand Council finance committee recommended by 8 votes to 7 rejecting the 2027 budget, which shows a 356.9-million-franc deficit.", "url": "https://www.vd.ch/actualites/communiques-de-presse-de-letat-de-vaud/detail/communique/projet-du-budget-2027-la-cofin-a-termine-ses-travaux-et-recommande-un-refus-en-vote-final", "source_domain": "vd.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Vaud cantonal parliament's finance committee (COFIN) recommended rejecting the canton's 2027 budget in the final vote, by 8 votes to 7, it said on Thursday 19 November, even though it backed opening the debate by 13 to 1. With the government's and the committee's amendments, the draft shows a deficit of 356.9 million francs. The no side came from three different directions. The Socialists and Greens say the cuts are unfairly shared and want more tax fairness; the Ensemble à Gauche–POP member wants past cuts reversed and new revenue; and the Green Liberals say the government still has no credible plan to balance the books. The FDP (PLR) and SVP (UDC) members accept the amended budget and oppose any new taxes or shifting costs to municipalities. The government revised its September draft in October after voters approved the so-called 12% initiative.", "why": "the Grand Council can still pass the budget, and the Socialists and Greens say they could change their vote if their proposals advance. But a recommendation to reject puts Vaud's finances, and the services and municipal transfers they pay for, in doubt weeks before the year starts.", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-vaud-committee-urges-rejecting-2027-budget", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-19", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Vaud", "COFIN", "Grand Council of Vaud"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-premium-rises-trim-swiss-disposable-income", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "Premium rises trim Swiss disposable income", "summary": "The FSO said 2026 health-premium increases cut average disposable income growth by 0.2 percentage points; basic premiums rose 4.3%.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/qAbDPn4NMLOe", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "health"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Rising health-insurance premiums slowed the growth of Swiss households' average disposable income by 0.2 percentage points between 2025 and 2026, the Federal Statistical Office (FSO) said on Friday 20 November. Basic compulsory premiums rose 4.3% in 2026, while supplementary insurance premiums were broadly unchanged, so the combined premium index rose 3.3%. Disposable income is what remains after taxes and insurance contributions for spending and saving.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-premium-rises-trim-swiss-disposable-income", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Statistical Office", "Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-outside-prosecutor-for-geneva-g7-kettle-complain", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "Outside prosecutor for Geneva G7 kettle complaints", "summary": "Geneva prosecutors will ask for an extraordinary out-of-canton prosecutor to handle complaints over the 14 June anti-G7 police kettle.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/suisse/geneve/un-procureur-extraordinaire-sera-designe-pour-instruire-les-plaintes-liees-a-la-nasse-du-g7", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Geneva's public prosecutor's office will ask for an extraordinary prosecutor from outside the canton to handle the criminal complaints over the police \"kettle\" at the end of the anti-G7 demonstration on 14 June, it confirmed on Friday 20 November. 549 people were held on the Quai Wilson for several hours. Complainants allege abuse of authority and unlawful detention, and their lawyer had asked for the ordinary prosecutor's office to step aside. Geneva has used extraordinary prosecutors since 2022 when there is a risk of apparent bias or a conflict of interest.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-outside-prosecutor-for-geneva-g7-kettle-complain", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Geneva", "G7", "Ministère public de Genève"]}
{"id": "2026-11-20-news-cassis-to-meet-wang-yi-in-nanjing", "date": "2026-11-20", "stream": "news", "headline": "Cassis to meet Wang Yi in Nanjing", "summary": "Ignazio Cassis will hold the fifth Swiss-Chinese strategic dialogue with Wang Yi in Nanjing on 23 November.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/xehRuIhGRpxx", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Foreign minister Ignazio Cassis will meet China's foreign minister Wang Yi in Nanjing on Monday 23 November for the fifth round of the Swiss–Chinese strategic dialogue, the foreign ministry said on Friday 20 November. Human rights and mediation are on the agenda along with trade, science and culture. The visit follows the signing of the upgraded Swiss–Chinese free-trade agreement by President Guy Parmelin and Xi Jinping on 30 October.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-20-news-cassis-to-meet-wang-yi-in-nanjing", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-20", "event_date": "2026-11-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ignazio Cassis", "Wang Yi", "China", "Switzerland"]}
